      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Those symptoms can be unsettling, but eye strain is unlikely to cause cobweb-like visual distortions. The blur or dots you're seeing are more likely related to an underlying issue, such as a visual disturbance, muscle imbalance, or minor ocular problems like blepharospasm. Considering eye strain typically affects one eye at a time and causes more general discomfort like fatigue, it's possible that your issue is something else. I would recommend consulting an eye doctor to rule out any underlying conditions.",
